rep("its short line is a ladder rung (사다리 발판) until the ledger-lines chapter;",
    "its short line is a ladder rung (사다리 발판) until the ledger-lines chapter, which names it a\n   LEDGER LINE (덧줄; 'leger' accepted): the rungs of a ladder up into the bird's sky over Queensland and down into the\n   turtle's sea under Kingsland, read from five Cs -- Sea C, Kingsland C, Clara's C, Queensland C, Sky C (Phase 428);")
row = """| 428 | 2026-10-11 | **Chapter 6 (Ledger Lines) APPLIED (her 20:58 'G1-3 너가 말한거 다 해당 / 너가 검토한거 책 바탕으로 최적으로 만들어줘' = every B as recommended in the Phase 427 pack).** patch428.py + ll428.jsx (in _workspace/chapter-review/g428/x). (1) Lesson Book, 7 pages, no draft marks: B1 ledger line (leger in the Teacher copy), B2 the ladder into the sky and the sea, B3 Sky C and Sea C, B4 up to three rungs, B5 no A C E lists in the book, B6 Between the lands kept, B9 the minimal opener; 'Clara's C sits on one rung, seen from either land'; Korean 1번/2번/3번 발판 throughout. (2) The app lesson is the book on screen (LedgerLearn = llLbPages(true), LL_STORE) with new moving parts: LlRungs (add rungs one at a time, check: a gap / one too many / neat, notes that need none), LlClimb (the ladder out of Queensland from F, out of Kingsland from G, drawn behind you; Sky C / Sea C named), LlTwins (A B C D E between the lands, seen from both lands + the keys), LlFiveCs (the five Cs to tap; the C hop with its explanation). (3) The drill has her 7 levels (B7): one rung Queensland, one rung Kingsland, two rungs both lands, Sky C and Sea C a step or a skip, between the lands, up to three rungs fast (Grade 2), keys (exact octave, the 3-octave keyboard); answers say where in the lands' words (llPlace: 'on rung 2 over Queensland', '= Kingsland's top line'). (4) Toolbox: the four tool ids now open the moving parts (Climb out of the lands, The five Cs, Between the lands, Draw the rungs), Korean too. The old LedgerLearn tools, explanations, LadderPic, ledgerDesc/staffPlace and the Phase 298 Workbook/Teacher copy are gone. (5) Workbook (B8, 6 pages): p2 Neat or not? (✓✗ ✓ ✗ ✗ mixed) / Draw the rungs (some need none) / How many rungs? (0-3, bare notes) ; p3 Fill the ladder (draw the missing notes A C E with rungs) / Name the sky notes / Words in the sky BADGE, CAGE ; p4 the same down into the sea, BEAD, CAFE ; p5 The same key in the other land (B D A into Kingsland, D E B into Queensland) / Read the borrowed rungs / Same key? (yes no no yes) ; p6 Hop from a C (circle the turtle, Clara or the bird) / Read them fast / the secret message CABBAGE ; p7 the check-up on paper (A draw the rungs, B sky, C sea, D between the lands, E hop from a C). LedgerTeacher (2 pages, every answer with the Workbook's own numbers -- tcAns takes a first number; the four lists and AMEB levels in one line). Paper notes may carry their own rungs (PaperStaff: rungs, rungC; room for every rung; no line through a bare note's hole off the staff). (6) All books: 'In this chapter' in Korean (이 챕터에서는), the check page says 'colour a circle' like its foot line; chapter 5's map names the lands in Korean. (7) Guide page lessons/ledger-lines.html (--final): her G1 (counting the rungs wrong, a note under the treble staff read as a bass note, lines too long or too far apart) and G2 (count out first, then the five Cs by heart) in 'From the teacher'; the parent tip (G3) written from the book -- the five Cs, the C hop, the drill; drawings from the book (guide428svg.js); worksheet = Workbook page 2 (lessons/img/ledger-lines-worksheet.jpg); room 6 lit on the guides' front page (house redrawn, sharing picture, 'Open rooms' card), sitemap; the printables card shows the same page (pages=1). Two fresh-eyes reviewers: music (draft) and the whole chapter -- every answer right; fixed: the 'nearest C' rule made exact, 'a little wider', the no-gap cross, a clipped extra rung, the sea words' boxes under the A, garbled Teacher places, the Workbook's numbers in the answers, 'left to right' for the message, the ladders and pairs no longer copy the book's pictures, answers varied, words numbered on, bigger drawing cells. Checks: ll428test 69/69 (new), ws419 45/45, ch1 21/21, ch2 21/21, ch3 35/35, sf405 22/22, no-song 24/24, lbcheck chapters 1-6 0 overflow en/ko, wbcheck chapter 6 0 overflow / 0 clipping en/ko. PDF: Claude outputs/Chapter-06-Ledger-Lines-v1.pdf (side by side + Teacher copy, 15 pages). Still open: Korean keep-all line breaking (asked, app-wide); chapter 5's guide page waits for its G1-G3. |
"""
i = s.index('| 427 | 2026-10-10 |'); j = s.index('\n', i) + 1
s = s[:j] + row + s[j:]
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s); print('CLAUDE.md ok')
